Labelling happens accross edges

`connected_components.connect_labels_in_matrix()` connects labels accross edges

All tests inside `test_launch_packmem2.py` fail.
    The new algorithm finds more defects since `matrix.fill_matrix()` no longer uses
    shifted indices produced by `matrix.check_edges()`.

The core logic of raidus-cell overlap is not defined rigorously anywhere.
The last row/column of cells expands beyond the box. The fixed cell size grid makes it
impossible to align the two. Defects at the edge are therefore ill defined and assigned.
If the box size varies sufficiently accross frames this effect is averaged out.

Another approach is to skip the periodic image interaction and use a grid that is
`MAX_GRID_SEARCH_CELLS` smaller than the box border on all sides. Defect size is best
estimated using periodic images however.